🎓 Key Concepts Explained
1. Role Directory Structure
text

role_name/
├── tasks/       # 🎯 What the role does
├── handlers/    # 🔄 Triggered actions
├── templates/   # 📝 Jinja2 templates
├── files/       # 📄 Static files
├── vars/        # 📊 High-priority variables
├── defaults/    # ⚙️ Low-priority defaults
└── meta/        # 📋 Dependencies & info

2. Variable Precedence (Most Important!)
text

Lowest Priority
    ↓
  role defaults     (roles/X/defaults/main.yml)
  inventory vars    (group_vars/all.yml)
  playbook vars     (vars in playbook)
  role vars         (roles/X/vars/main.yml)
  host vars         (host_vars/hostname.yml)
  extra vars        (-e "key=value")
    ↓
Highest Priority

3. Task Inclusion Types
yaml

# Static import - processed at playbook parse time
- import_tasks: static.yml
  when: condition  # ❌ Doesn't work - imported always

# Dynamic include - processed at runtime
- include_tasks: dynamic.yml
  when: condition  # ✅ Works - included only if condition true

4. Role Dependencies
yaml

# roles/nginx/meta/main.yml
dependencies:
  - role: common          # Run common before nginx
  - role: ssl             # Run ssl before nginx
    vars:                 # Pass variables to dependency
      ssl_cert_path: /etc/nginx/ssl

5. Tags Strategy
yaml

# In role tasks:
- name: Install packages
  ansible.builtin.apt:
    name: nginx
  tags: 
    - nginx       # Role-specific
    - install     # Action type
    - packages    # Category

# Usage:
ansible-playbook site.yml --tags "nginx,install"
ansible-playbook site.yml --skip-tags "monitoring
